What do humans know of those?

268
00:14:53,480 --> 00:14:55,640
Don't speak such words to me, girl!

269
00:14:56,680 --> 00:14:58,920
Oh, you've done it now, human.

270
00:14:58,920 --> 00:15:02,760
You may think there's strength in numbers, but that's just an illusion.

271
00:15:02,760 --> 00:15:04,440
You have no hope!

272
00:15:04,620 --> 00:15:06,700
I won't lose to you, humans!

273
00:15:07,060 --> 00:15:09,160
Your lives belong to me!

274
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:14,160
In the end, I think maybe he was the one who despaired the most.

275
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:24,220
Hey, kid, you're an idiot, right?

276
00:15:24,460 --> 00:15:24,660
Huh?

277
00:15:25,940 --> 00:15:27,980
I said you're an idiot, aren't you?

278
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:30,480
Answer me, or I'll mess you up.

279
00:15:31,480 --> 00:15:33,500
Yes, I'm an idiot, Captain Yami, sir!

280
00:15:33,720 --> 00:15:36,880
An idiot doesn't have to think too deep about that kind of stuff.

281
00:15:37,020 --> 00:15:37,400
Got it!

282
00:15:39,700 --> 00:15:39,940
Huh?

283
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:43,320
You just focus on following your dream.

284
00:15:45,560 --> 00:15:46,220
That's it?

285
00:15:46,540 --> 00:15:47,140
My dream?

286
00:15:48,060 --> 00:15:49,080
For now, anyway.

287
00:15:49,080 --> 00:15:51,780
I can't see it!

288
00:15:51,780 --> 00:15:53,480
I can't pull my headband back up!

289
00:15:53,920 --> 00:15:55,740
Come on, I've got two broken arms, remember?

290
00:15:56,200 --> 00:15:56,960
Hey, Captain!

291
00:15:57,400 --> 00:15:59,020
Where are you going, sir?

292
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:01,860
You can't just leave me here!

293
00:16:08,940 --> 00:16:12,060
For now, all I have to do is follow my dream.

294
00:16:13,020 --> 00:16:13,500
Huh.

295
00:16:13,500 --> 00:16:17,580
My dream, except it's not just mine.

296
00:16:21,740 --> 00:16:22,900
Check it out, you know!

297
00:16:22,980 --> 00:16:24,880
I got a snazzy new grimoire!

298
00:16:25,280 --> 00:16:28,340
Okay, it's a little beat up, but I'll treasure it all my life anyway!

299
00:16:28,640 --> 00:16:29,300
I will!

300
00:16:29,300 --> 00:16:40,260
I will repay my debt one day.

301
00:16:42,640 --> 00:16:44,680
Asta, we made a promise.

302
00:16:46,080 --> 00:16:47,240
Do you remember it?

303
00:16:47,240 --> 00:16:50,480
So you want to be the Wizard King, too?

304
00:16:51,220 --> 00:16:52,740
That means...

305
00:16:52,740 --> 00:16:54,180
You know, Asta?

306
00:16:54,680 --> 00:16:55,980
You are my rival!

307
00:16:57,860 --> 00:17:00,300
I actually can't believe you remember it.

308
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:03,600
The way you've been acting lately, I was pretty sure you'd forgotten.

309
00:17:05,300 --> 00:17:08,220
Like I'd be friendly with someone I consider my rival.

310
00:17:08,220 --> 00:17:16,060
You showed me it was possible, gave me hope, that even though we're poor orphans,

311
00:17:16,740 --> 00:17:21,320
commoners, we can still make something of ourselves in this world.

312
00:17:22,280 --> 00:17:23,480
And to prove that?

313
00:17:23,620 --> 00:17:26,040
To make Sister Lily and everybody else happy.

314
00:17:26,040 --> 00:17:35,320
We'll fight to see who will be the Wizard King.

315
00:17:35,700 --> 00:17:36,780
Whatever it takes.

316
00:17:43,920 --> 00:17:44,860
Not yet.

317
00:17:45,420 --> 00:17:46,100
Not yet.

318
00:17:46,600 --> 00:17:49,020
I'm nowhere near as powerful as I need to be.

319
00:17:49,700 --> 00:17:51,160
Yuno's got the lead for now.

320
00:17:51,920 --> 00:17:53,780
The captain was totally right!

321
00:17:54,100 --> 00:17:55,880
I'm just gonna follow my own dream!

322
00:17:56,040 --> 00:17:57,080
Yeah, that's it!

323
00:17:57,520 --> 00:17:58,720
My arms are gonna heal!

324
00:17:59,240 --> 00:18:01,220
I'll get stronger than I've ever been!

325
00:18:01,540 --> 00:18:03,320
And then I'll become the Wizard King!

326
00:18:07,620 --> 00:18:10,100
Magic Knight!

327
00:18:10,400 --> 00:18:11,640
Really fantastic!

328
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:13,020
Thank you!

329
00:18:15,320 --> 00:18:17,440
How long are they gonna thank us for?

330
00:18:17,440 --> 00:18:18,640
Sure are energetic.

331
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:20,040
Maybe too much.

332
00:18:20,620 --> 00:18:23,020
Nothing wrong with a little gratitude, if you ask me.

333
00:18:23,780 --> 00:18:25,060
And look at the ladies!

334
00:18:25,340 --> 00:18:25,760
Beautiful!

335
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:28,720
Oh, good.

336
00:18:29,240 --> 00:18:30,940
Go on, eat them!

337
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:37,940
Well, see ya.

338
00:18:38,340 --> 00:18:39,560
And thanks for everything.

339
00:18:40,100 --> 00:18:41,500
Please come back anytime.

340
00:18:42,080 --> 00:18:43,700
You're always welcome here.

341
00:18:44,240 --> 00:18:45,200
Yeah, come back!

342
00:18:45,440 --> 00:18:45,820
Okay?

343
00:18:45,820 --> 00:18:51,600
I'm the strongest of all the mages in the Underwater Temple, and I never got to show off my moves!

344
00:18:52,100 --> 00:18:55,680
So, uh, how are the captured Midnight Sun minions holding up?

345
00:18:55,680 --> 00:19:01,740
They're screaming a bunch, but they can't go anywhere, so I'm not really worried about it.

346
00:19:02,580 --> 00:19:06,300
Man, that is a seriously strong binding spell you've got there.

347
00:19:06,300 --> 00:19:07,300
Huh, guess I never crossed my mind.

348
00:19:07,300 --> 00:19:08,440
Guess I never crossed my mind.

349
00:19:08,760 --> 00:19:10,060
Just keep at it, alright?

350
00:19:10,480 --> 00:19:12,200
I know your dreams will come true someday.

351
00:19:13,040 --> 00:19:15,520
There's gotta be a spell that can heal your leg and your throat.

352
00:19:16,300 --> 00:19:19,020
I'll work hard too, and get my arms all fixed up!

353
00:19:19,020 --> 00:19:22,020
I'll be dancing on this leg again in no time.

354
00:19:28,300 --> 00:19:30,040
Asta, thank you.

355
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:32,040
I'm never gonna give up either.

356
00:19:32,040 --> 00:19:36,840
Okay, let's go.

357
00:19:36,940 --> 00:19:37,520
